def build_prompt(o):
    """o = one RegMap row. Returns the prompt. {{ }} become { } in the f-string."""
    return f"""You are a senior US regulatory compliance analyst reviewing Regulation Z (Truth in Lending, 12 CFR 1026).
Your output will be read by senior compliance and risk stakeholders.

TASK
Assess whether ONE HSBC RegMap obligation is covered by the vendor-identified obligations listed below.

WHICH VENDOR OBLIGATIONS COUNT AS "COVERING" (be strict)
Include a vendor obligation ONLY if it states a requirement that forms part of THIS RegMap obligation.
Vendors often split one rule across several rows - include every such row - but EXCLUDE:
  - general, definitional or framework rules that merely apply to many obligations
    (e.g. general disclosure form/timing rules) unless the RegMap text itself contains that requirement;
  - rows whose scope differs (e.g. RegMap is home-secured open-end credit, vendor row is
    non-home-secured or closed-end) - these are NOT covering;
  - rows that are only thematically related.
Judge mainly on the meaning of the text. Citations are supporting evidence only: a matching citation
alone is not sufficient, and a different citation does not rule a match out.

COVERAGE STATUS
  FULL    = all material elements of the RegMap obligation are covered
  PARTIAL = the core requirement is covered but one or more material elements are missing or different
  NONE    = no vendor obligation addresses the core requirement

GAPS / DIFFERENCES
Return a list of separate points. Check: obligated party, required/prohibited action, scope,
conditions/triggers, timing, numeric thresholds, exceptions, other material details.
Each point has:
  "type": one of
     "Covered"           - one point only, summarising what the vendor obligations do cover
     "Missing in Vendor" - a RegMap requirement absent from / different in the vendor obligations
     "Missing in RegMap" - a material vendor requirement absent from the RegMap text
     "Structural"        - e.g. one RegMap obligation distributed across several vendor rows
  "point":    one professional sentence describing it
  "evidence": the supporting wording in double quotes, naming its source and citation, e.g.
     RegMap (1026.6(a)) states "..." ; vendor ecfr....a.2 (1026.6(a)(2)) states "..." / is silent.
Rules:
- Always start with one "Covered" point (or, if status is NONE, a "Missing in Vendor" point).
- If nothing is missing, the only points are "Covered" (and "Structural" if relevant).
- Every Missing point MUST have quoted evidence.
- NEVER give recommendations, next steps or suggestions. NEVER mention scores or ratings.

IF STATUS IS NONE
Fill "nearest_thematic" with one sentence naming the closest related vendor rules with citations, e.g.
"Nearest thematic vendor rules concern ... (1026.x(y)) but do not address ..."
Leave "covering_vendor_ids" empty.

STRICT RULES
- Only use vendor obligation IDs from the list. Never invent IDs.

REGMAP OBLIGATION
ID: {o['Obligation ID']}
Citation: {o['Obligation Citation']}
Title: {o['Obligation Title']}
Text: {o['Obligation Detailed Text']}

VENDOR OBLIGATIONS
{vendor_block}

Return ONLY valid JSON (no markdown) in exactly this shape:
{{
  "covering_vendor_ids": ["ecfr....", "ecfr...."],
  "coverage_status": "FULL|PARTIAL|NONE",
  "gaps": [
    {{"type": "Covered", "point": "...", "evidence": "..."}},
    {{"type": "Missing in Vendor", "point": "...", "evidence": "RegMap (1026.x) states \\"...\\"; the vendor obligations are silent."}}
  ],
  "nearest_thematic": ""
}}"""

